  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 33,
    "summary": "Rejoice in the Lord—Sing unto Him a new song—He loves righteousness and judgment—Blessed is the nation whose God is the Lord.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Rejoice in the Lord, O ye righteous: for praise is comely for the upright.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "Ps. 147:1; Alma 26:8; D&C 136:28 (28–29)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Praise the Lord with harp: sing unto him with the psaltery and an instrument of ten strings.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Sing unto him a new song; play skilfully with a loud noise.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "IE raise also fresh, new praises and thanks to God for His ever-new blessings. Ps. 40:3; D&C 25:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the word of the Lord is right; and all his works are done in truth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "D&C 84:45."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 27
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He loveth righteousness and judgment: the earth is full of the goodness of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "HEB justice."
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "Ps. 119:64."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "By the word of the Lord were the heavens made; and all the host of them by the breath of his mouth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "See JST John 1:1–16 (Appendix). TG Jesus Christ, Creator."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Heaven."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He gathereth the waters of the sea together as an heap: he layeth up the depth in storehouses.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let all the earth fear the Lord: let all the inhabitants of the world stand in awe of him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For he spake, and it was done; he commanded, and it stood fast.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "Gen. 1:3; Ps. 148:5 (5–6); 2 Cor. 4:6; D&C 38:3; Moses 2:5 (4–5)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 30
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord bringeth the counsel of the heathen to nought: he maketh the devices of the people of none effect.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "Neh. 4:15."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "HEB nations, Gentiles. TG Heathen."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The counsel of the Lord standeth for ever, the thoughts of his heart to all generations.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "2 Ne. 9:16; D&C 1:38 (37–39); Moses 1:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Blessed is the nation whose God is the Lord; and the people whom he hath chosen for his own inheritance.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "Moses 1:26 (25–26)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 34
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 64
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord looketh from heaven; he beholdeth all the sons of men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "From the place of his habitation he looketh upon all the inhabitants of the earth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "Isa. 63:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He fashioneth their hearts alike; he considereth all their works.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "1 Ne. 15:33 (26–36); 3 Ne. 27:25 (23–27)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There is no king saved by the multitude of an host: a mighty man is not delivered by much strength.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Ps. 44:6; 2 Ne. 4:34."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "An horse is a vain thing for safety: neither shall he deliver any by his great strength.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "Prov. 21:31."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "Amos 2:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 11
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, the eye of the Lord is upon them that fear him, upon them that hope in his mercy;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Ps. 34:15; 1 Pet. 3:12; D&C 1:1; 38:7 (7–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 30
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To deliver their soul from death, and to keep them alive in famine.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "Ps. 37:19 (18–19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Our soul waiteth for the Lord: he is our help and our shield.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "Deut. 33:29 (26–29); D&C 35:14 (13–14)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For our heart shall rejoice in him, because we have trusted in his holy name.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let thy mercy, O Lord, be upon us, according as we hope in thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Hope."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
